  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "convoport",
      "text": "**DeepSeek Harness plugin: auto-capture your DeepSeek web conversations, store them 100% locally, import selected messages into workspace sessions, and see how many tokens you've saved.**\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/convoport)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/convoport)\n[](LICENSE)\n\n[中文说明](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "| Capability | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Auto-capture** | Companion MV3 browser extension watches `chat.deepseek.com`, pulls conversations via the official `history_messages` API, and syncs them to this plugin automatically. |\n| **Local storage** | Data lives in `$DSH_HOME/capture/` (JSON, one file per conversation + `index.json`). **Zero upload** — and it's plain JSON, readable by any developer. |\n| **Token savings stats** | Cumulative tokens saved / conversation count / today's captures / estimated savings (with the counting method stated on the page). |\n| **Message-level import** | Don't import whole conversations — open a capture, **check individual messages** (quick-select \"first 3 / last 3\"), then import = **create a new Harness session** in the current workspace with those messages as its history. Continue chatting from there. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "```\nBrowser extension (MV3)                dsh plugin (this repo)\n┌──────────────────────┐   POST   ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ content script       │ ────────▶ │ lib/index.js  server half    │\n│ · chat.deepseek.com  │ /capture │ · /capture/ingest    ingest   │"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Install the plugin",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add convoport"
    },
    {
      "section": "is http://127.0.0.1:3080 (the dsh web port).",
      "text": "```\n\n> Note: Chrome deliberately blocks command-line loading of unpacked extensions;\n> the manual \"Load unpacked\" step above is required (it's the standard flow)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "1. With the extension enabled, just chat on `chat.deepseek.com` — the extension syncs automatically.\n2. A \"⛁ Convoport\" button appears at the bottom of the Web sidebar:\n   - Stat cards: total tokens saved / conversations / today's captures / estimated savings\n   - Capture list: title, message count, tokens, import status\n3. Click a conversation → **message-level picker**: check the messages you want (quick-select \"first 3 / last 3 / all / clear\").\n4. Click \"Import selected → new session (N)\" — a new session appears in the sidebar; its history is exactly the messages you picked. Continue chatting there."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "A `/capture` command also shows the stats overview right in the chat."
    },
    {
      "section": "API",
      "text": "| Method | Path | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| POST | `/capture/ingest` | Extension reports a conversation `{source,url,title,captured_at,messages[]}`; idempotent merge by url, dedup by message_id |\n| GET | `/capture/sessions` | Capture asset list (with import status) |\n| GET | `/capture/messages?id=` | Full messages of one capture |\n| GET | `/capture/stats` | Stats |\n| GET | `/capture/search?q=` | Full-text search (SQLite FTS5 + LIKE fallback) |\n| POST | `/capture/import` | `{id, indexes[]}` → create a new Harness session, returns `sessionId` |\n| DELETE | `/capture/sessions?id=` | Delete a capture |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Token accounting",
      "text": "- Prefers DeepSeek's official `accumulated_token_count` (the extension writes per-message `token_count`).\n- Falls back to the Harness-style heuristic: 4 chars/token + structural overhead (same as `dsh-token-meter`).\n- The stats page/command output always states the method; estimated savings use a `$0.02 / 1k tokens` reference price."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "then run:",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add convoport   # triggers reconcile\n```\n\nServer-side changes (`lib/index.js`) require restarting `dsh web`; client-side\n(`lib/client.js`) is read live without cache — just refresh the browser."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test              # all suites except extension-e2e\nnpm run test:e2e      # extension→plugin full chain (needs dsh web running)\nnpm run pack:check    # inspect what npm pack would publish\n```"
    }
  ],
